title: Universality
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
wikipedia: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universality_(philosophy)

The idea that universal facts exist and can be progressively discovered, as opposed to relativism, which asserts that all facts are merely relative to one's perspective. Absolutism and relativism have been explored at length in contemporary analytic philosophy.

Related: [[Absolutism]]

